course: dictionary
lesson: 14166
title: Mocha: a drink, a colour and a place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one. «Dad ordered a mocha at the café and sipped it slowly.» The clues are ordered, café and sipped, so mocha means a drink. Always ask: which meaning fits the words around it?
explain: «The cake had a rich mocha flavour, with coffee and chocolate together.» The clues are flavour, coffee and chocolate. Mocha here means a taste that mixes coffee and chocolate. Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you have probably got it.
explain: «Her new coat was a soft mocha colour, like milky coffee.» Here mocha describes the colour of the coat. The clue like milky coffee tells you it is a mid-brown shade. Mocha can also be a place name, as in «Coffee was first traded from the port of Mocha in Yemen.»
fact: Mocha can be a noun (a drink, a flavour, a place) or an adjective (a colour), so check the words around it.
fact: «Mocha» means a coffee drink made with chocolate, hot milk and espresso.
fact: «Mocha» also means a mid-brown colour, like milky coffee.
fact: Mocha was the name of a famous coffee port in Yemen, also called al-Mukha.
fact: A mocha flavour mixes coffee and chocolate, as in mocha cake or mocha ice cream.
exercise: «Dad ordered a mocha at the café.» What is a mocha here? | A small brown bird | A bright red shirt | *A coffee drink made with chocolate and hot milk | A type of sports ball
exercise: «Her new coat was a soft mocha colour.» What does mocha mean here? | *A mid-brown colour like milky coffee | A bright red colour | A pale, shiny silver | A loud pattern
exercise: «Coffee was first traded from the port of Mocha in Yemen.» In this sentence, what kind of word is Mocha? | *A place name, a port in Yemen | A drink | A type of cake | A colour
test: «The mocha cake was rich and chocolatey.» What flavour does mocha suggest? | Fresh mint | Plain vanilla | *Coffee mixed with chocolate | Lemon and sugar
test: «Lily wore mocha boots with her blue dress.» What colour are the boots? | *Mid-brown | Pure white | Sky blue | Bright pink
exam: «Can I have a mocha latte, please?» Which meaning of mocha fits best? | *A coffee drink | A loud noise | A bright green | A town in England
